    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0055" n="45" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg45"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/2438: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-09T15:00:00-04:00">May 9, 1942—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>375. Your 529, May 8, 5 p.m. For your strictly confidential information only: We
                    concur in your opinion that nothing should be <pb facs="0056" n="46"
                        xml:id="pg46"/> done in any way that might arouse the slightest suspicion on
                    the part of the Chinese of any lack of confidence in them and have accordingly
                    taken up the matter with General Marshall. He shares this view, and it is
                    understood that the War Department will immediately send appropriate
                    instructions in the matter to General Magruder.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d54-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
